# ElevenLabs Voice Agent Project Rules

Description: Guidelines for developing a Next.js application with ElevenLabs Conversational AI
Globs: **/*.tsx **/*.ts **/*.js **/*.jsx

## Project Overview

This project creates a voice-based conversational AI interface using ElevenLabs' client library within a Next.js framework. The application allows users to interact with AI agents through voice, handling both input (microphone) and output (speech) in real-time.

## Key Technologies

- Next.js 15.3+ with App Router
- TypeScript
- ElevenLabs Conversational AI (@11labs/client)
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- WebSocket for real-time communication
- Web Audio API for audio processing

## Architecture Guidelines

### Core Components

- **VoiceAgent Component**: Client-side component handling the conversation lifecycle, audio visualization, and UI controls
- **API Routes**: Server endpoints for handling authentication and signed URL generation
- **Utility Functions**: Audio processing and state management helpers
- **Environment Variables**: Secure storage of API keys and agent IDs

### File Organization

- `/app`: Main application code using Next.js App Router
  - `/components`: Reusable UI components
  - `/api`: Server-side API routes
  - `/utils`: Helper utilities
  - `/hooks`: Custom React hooks

### Coding Standards

- Prefer functional components with hooks over class components
- Use TypeScript interfaces for all props and state
- Handle all audio permissions explicitly and gracefully
- Implement proper error boundaries for audio processing failures
- Use React's useEffect cleanup functions to prevent memory leaks
- Implement responsive design for all components

## State Management

- Use React context for global state when needed
- Prefer local component state for UI-specific state
- Handle WebSocket connection state with clear status indicators

## Audio Processing Requirements

- Request microphone permissions before initializing conversation
- Provide visual feedback of audio input/output levels
- Handle volume adjustments through the ElevenLabs client API
- Implement graceful reconnection if connection is lost

## Error Handling

- Provide clear user feedback for:
  - Microphone permission denials
  - Connection failures
  - API errors
  - Audio processing issues
- Log errors for debugging but protect sensitive information

## Security Considerations

- Never expose API keys in client-side code
- Implement proper authentication for private agents
- Use server-side API routes to generate signed URLs
- Follow Next.js best practices for environment variable handling

## Performance Guidelines

- Minimize unnecessary re-renders in audio visualization components
- Optimize WebSocket data handling
- Consider using Web Workers for intensive audio processing
- Implement lazy loading for non-critical components

## Testing Approach

- Write unit tests for utility functions
- Create integration tests for the conversation flow
- Test audio processing with mock audio streams
- Verify error handling paths

## Documentation Standards

- Include JSDoc comments for all functions and components
- Document props with TypeScript interfaces
- Add usage examples in component documentation
- Document environment variables requirements